{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01XmDQTgTsCVAaATqeFFzGWY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **Q22: Two models, same accuracy, different confidence — which choose? Calibration?**\n\nThe note covers:\n\n- **Concept** — Calibration aligns predicted confidence with empirical accuracy; ECE (Expected Calibration Error) is the key metric\n- **Mechanism** — Reliability diagrams (confidence vs accuracy bins), identifying overconfident vs underconfident models, and three recalibration techniques: Platt scaling, **temperature scaling** (Guo et al. 2017, the neural-net default), and isotonic regression\n- **Example** — Content moderation system: two models at 87% accuracy, but ECE 0.03 vs 0.14 — the miscalibrated model auto-approves policy violations with false 92% confidence and floods the HITL queue with the wrong cases\n- **Decision table** — when calibration matters (HITL triggers, auto-approve gates) vs when accuracy/AUC is sufficient (ranking)\n- **Pitfalls** — picking by AUC alone, treating calibration as fixed (it drifts under distribution shift), and misapplying Platt scaling to deep nets\n\nTwo items remain in the Next queue: Q23 and the validate run."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_read_input_tokens":68539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":294,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1053617c-11bf-4d31-a12e-715b58aabb82","uuid":"ce81f1dc-ef9d-49d8-a40d-b46f5ce6af91"}
